  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Well Body 4 Betteh Education</narrative>
  </title>
  <description>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">This project seeks to stimulate behaviour change leading to improved hygiene practices, increased   access to clean water, sanitation and quality education in rural communities in Bo District. It will also contribute to the response trajectory of the early recovery needs of targeted rural poor communities focusing on orphans, young persons and their families including victims of Ebola.  The project intends to respond to the following problems: inadequate and limited access to water supply, sanitation and hand washing facilities, unsafe water which leads to waterborne disease, young persons with poor hygiene and hand washing practices, lack of standard toilet facilities and poor and hindered access to education facilities and services. The planned actions will be done through community-led integrated approach leveraging on the community drive for change. A context analysis of our proposed target rural poor communities indicates the following:
1. Inadequate and limited access to water supply, sanitation and hand-washing facilities.
2. Young persons with poor hygiene and hand-washing practices.
3. Lack of standard toilet facilities.
4. Poor and hindered access to education facilities and services.</narrative>
  </description>
